          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:modify_unit",
            side: 1,
            facing: "se",
            filter: "%7B%22tag%22%3A%22filter%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%7B%22id%22%3A%22Chantal%22%7D%2C%22children%22%3A%5B%5D%7D",
            id: "Chantal",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:recall_unit",
            id: "Kalenz",
            unit: "Kalenz",
            x: 15,
            y: 1,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:delay",
            time: 500,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to",
            x: 10,
            y: 20,
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Kalenz",
            text: _("You have led us to a dark part of the jungle, great-granddaughter. And undead? What are undead doing in Wesmere?!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Chantal",
            text: _("Not any undead. That dark rider is our friend Deoran, risen anew as a wight after Eldred so cruelly struck him down. He remembers nothing but echoes. It is terrible, Kalenz!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Deoran",
            text: _("Death... I lowered my sword... A blade in my chest..."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Chantal",
            text: _("I don’t know whether Deoran was turned to undeath as some insult of Asheviere’s or by the dark magic of Eldred’s fall, but now he has come here to Wesmere. He has sought me out..."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Kalenz",
            text: _("Deoran was a good man, and deserved better than the end he met. I know you and he were close, Chantal, and I am sorry."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Chantal",
            text: _("I had not the heart to kill him... one death was enough pain. But I know that we cannot leave him to rampage through Wesmere. Now that you are here, if his bones must be crushed and his body destroyed, so be it."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Kalenz",
            text: _("Indeed, it would a mercy to put this cursed being out of his misery. But perhaps it can be done without the violence that you would so abhor."),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to",
            x: 4,
            y: 14,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to",
            x: 4,
            y: 14,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:add_item",
            x: 5,
            y: 15,
            item_name: "",
